{
  "name": "Find trending video ideas for your niche from Google Trends and YouTube with Gemini and Telegram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Find trending video ideas for your niche from Google Trends and YouTube with Gemini and Telegram\n\nWake up to a short list of video ideas that fit your niche and are timely today. Each morning the workflow reads Google Trends' daily trending searches for your country and the latest uploads from channels you watch, and Gemini picks only the ideas that match your niche and audience, with a hook, an angle and why now. Ideas are logged to Google Sheets and sent to Telegram. No API keys except Gemini: both sources are free public RSS feeds.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Set radar settings** holds your niche, audience, country code, channel IDs to watch, relevance bar and Telegram chat.\n2. Google Trends' RSS (`trends.google.com/trending/rss?geo=GB`) and each channel's YouTube RSS feed are read in parallel. A broken feed is skipped.\n3. **Collect signals** turns both into short text; uploads older than the lookback window are dropped.\n4. **Pick video ideas** asks Gemini for structured ideas scored 1-10 for relevance, and **Rank ideas** keeps the best.\n5. Ideas suggested on earlier days are skipped, new ones are appended to the `Ideas` sheet and sent as one Telegram digest.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add **Google Gemini (PaLM) API**, **Google Sheets** and **Telegram** credentials.\n2. Create a sheet with an `Ideas` tab: `idea_id, found_on, topic, hook, format, angle, why_now, source, relevance, urgency, audience, status`.\n3. In **Set radar settings**, add the Sheet ID and your channel IDs (they start with `UC`).\n4. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n- Raise `min_relevance` for fewer, sharper ideas, or change `geo` to any country code.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 980,
        "width": 600
      },
